            },
            "authorType": "COMMENT",
            "competitionRanking": 1219,
            "content": "<p>What was the batch size here? I am trying to understand how we can achieve that throughput.</p>",
            "feedbackTrackingData": {},
            "id": 3427584,
            "isThankYou": false,
            "kernelVersion": 0,
            "parent": {},
            "postDate": "2026-03-24T09:14:40.813Z",
            "rawMarkdown": "What was the batch size here? I am trying to understand how we can achieve that throughput.",
            "replies": [
              {
                "author": {
                  "displayName": "Tong Hui Kang",
                  "id": 1680925,
                  "progressionOptOut": false,
                  "thumbnailUrl": "https://storage.googleapis.com/kaggle-avatars/thumbnails/1680925-kg.jpg",
                  "tier": "MASTER",
                  "url": "/huikang"
                },
                "authorType": "TOPIC",
                "competitionRanking": 748,
                "content": "<p>For vLLM inference, we do not think in terms of batch size but in terms of concurrency <a href=\"https://docs.vllm.ai/en/stable/configuration/engine_args/#-max-num-seqs\" target=\"_blank\"><code>--max-num-seqs</code></a>.</p>\n<p>I remember having a concurrency of 256. I do not think I needed that high, I remember achieving the same 2.5k token throughput with a concurrency of 128.</p>",
                "feedbackTrackingData": {},
                "id": 3427624,
                "isThankYou": false,
                "kernelVersion": 0,
                "parent": {},
                "postDate": "2026-03-24T10:05:40.083Z",
                "rawMarkdown": "For vLLM inference, we do not think in terms of batch size but in terms of concurrency [`--max-num-seqs`](https://docs.vllm.ai/en/stable/configuration/engine_args/#-max-num-seqs).\n\nI remember having a concurrency of 256. I do not think I needed that high, I remember achieving the same 2.5k token throughput with a concurrency of 128.",
